> gurti paun
Nu E₂^gurti natta taruḫḫun pāun. Nu URUDU^dammurin natta ḫarkun.

Why exactly the narrator requires a dammuri-object is unclear. Presumably it
was so obvious to the ancient scribe that it did not need to be explained; but
to modern scholars, it remains a mystery. This is unfortunately quite a common
situation in ancient texts.

